{
  "version": 1,
  "note": "FR-322-AC-268 (TC-280 MU-25..MU-30): dimension equivalence over dimension nodes of three packages (the derived dimensions of XP-08..XP-10 name `terms` entries by node key, each a closed DimensionBody term). The reader that decides these outcomes is quire-contract-ir's (FR-063-AC-3, FR-063-AC-4); these vectors are authoritative for it and QSpec's test checks only their shape. Each node is a structural id {package,path,ordinal}; `form` is the node's scalar_type form (every node is a dimension except `rpc_s`, the unit XP-05 names). `pair` names two entries of `nodes`; root_scale is the exact positive rational for which one canonical root of the first equals root_scale canonical roots of the second. `at` is the index in `equivalences` of the refused node (the later in node-id order). The equivalence node's own id is assigned: path [scalar_type, dimension_equivalence, first id, second id] in package `example`, ordinal from the entry (default 0). Each `pair` entry is the exact wire operand of `dimension_node_ids` (FR-322-AC-299): a package operand `{package, node}` for a foreign dimension, or a plain node id for a local operand. The importing package is `example`; a case's `dependency_selections` (default `acme/clock`, `acme/flow`, `acme/rpc`) are its direct selections and `closure_only` names packages reachable only through a selection. A refusal at one operand (XP-05 the wrong-kind unit, XP-11 to XP-15) names the operand position `operand` (0 or 1), the pointer `/semantic_graph/nodes/{at node}/body/dimension_node_ids/{operand}`; a refusal at the equivalence node itself (XP-02 to XP-04, XP-06 to XP-09) has no `operand`. A refusal with a `code` (XP-11 to XP-15) names its `code`, `cause` (absent for XP-14), the equivalence index `at`, the operand position `operand` and, for the selection and name codes, the `member` (`package` or `node`) the refusal points at: `/semantic_graph/nodes/{at node}/body/dimension_node_ids/{operand}/{member}`. `form` `absent` marks a node the case names but its package does not declare (XP-12, XP-13).",
